# Line endings matter on this project.
#
# The host is Windows, but almost everything here is consumed by Linux: shell
# scripts run on the board or in WSL, patches are applied by `patch`, and init
# scripts are parsed by busybox. A CRLF sneaking into any of them produces
# failures that look like something else entirely -- this project has already
# lost time to `sed -i 's/\r$//'` being needed everywhere, and to a patch that
# silently matched nothing because the target file had CRLF.
#
# Force LF for everything the Linux side touches, regardless of core.autocrlf.
#
# Default: EVERY text file is LF in the working copy. The per-type rules below
# came first and missed types (*.config, Makefile, extensionless files outside
# the overlay): a clone on a machine with core.autocrlf=true checked 456 files
# out as CRLF, the kernel fragment among them.
*           text=auto eol=lf

*.sh        text eol=lf
*.py        text eol=lf
*.patch     text eol=lf
*.cfg       text eol=lf
*.opt       text eol=lf
*.conf      text eol=lf
*.dts       text eol=lf
*.dtsi      text eol=lf
*.c         text eol=lf
*.h         text eol=lf
*.mk        text eol=lf
*.in        text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf
*defconfig* text eol=lf
Config.in   text eol=lf

# init scripts and other extensionless files under the rootfs overlay
buildroot-external/board/*/rootfs_overlay/** text eol=lf

# Binaries: never touch.
*.png       binary
*.ttf       binary
*.so        binary
*.img       binary
*.vfat      binary
*.raw       binary
*.tar.gz    binary
*.bin       binary
*.dtb       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.xz        binary

# Upstream RetroArch asset that is CRLF in its own repository: keep it byte-exact.
buildroot-external/package/retroarch/retroarch/retro-assets/nxrgui/overlay/README.txt -text

# These patches target upstream files that are CRLF, so their hunk lines must
# carry CRLF too. Under "eol=lf" git normalised them and patch failed with
# "different line endings": RetroOPI_Z3 only built from its working copy (its
# index held LF versions), and a fresh tree (the K2B port) broke on all three.
buildroot-external/package/retroarch/libretro-atari800/0001-atari800-vkbd-on-R-as-well-as-L3.patch -text
buildroot-external/package/retroarch/libretro-fbalpha/0001-pgm-Support-threaded-draw-and-bind-it-to-cpu-0.patch -text
buildroot-external/package/retroarch/libretro-mame2010/0001-Skip-cpu-settings-for-buildroot.patch -text
